  "text": "He sentenced her to be burned alive. Then she sent back his ID. Genesis thirty-eight. Tamar marries Judah's oldest son. He dies. By custom she goes to the next brother. He dies too. Judah has a third son, Shelah. He tells Tamar to go live as a widow at her father's house until the boy grows up. Then never sends for her. She is parked. No husband. No children. No standing. No legal way to fight it. Years pass. Shelah grows up and nobody comes. So she takes off her widow's clothes, covers herself with a veil, and sits by the road to Timnath. Judah goes past, does not recognise her, and propositions her. And here she gets sharp. He offers a young goat. She says, \"Wilt thou give me a pledge, till thou send it?\" He says, what pledge. And she names three things. His signet. His bracelets. His staff. That is his identification. She took his ID. Three months later word gets to Judah that she is pregnant. And he says, \"Bring her forth, and let her be burnt.\" And she sends him his own signet and staff with a message. \"Discern, I pray thee, whose are these.\" And Judah says it out loud, in front of everybody. \"She hath been more righteous than I.\"",
